industry:enza:JR105753.description:
Strong financial leadership helps Enza Zaden turn commercial opportunities into sustainable growth. As Global Finance Business Partner Marketing & Sales and Mid Tech, you will work directly with senior management on strategy, performance, and value creation. You will combine financial expertise with international collaboration and have the opportunity to improve decision-making across the business.
 Make a difference as Global Finance Business Partner 
As Global Finance Business Partner, you will be the strategic financial partner for Marketing & Sales and the cross-functional Business Dynamic Mid Tech. You will be part of both management teams and report to the Head of Business Control. You will translate financial and commercial insights into clear choices for growth, improvement, and value creation. You will work globally with senior management, Business Controllers, and Finance Managers. In this role, your work will include:
 Taking responsibility for value creation, strategy definition and execution, and performance as a member of both management teams;
 Advising, challenging, and supporting the Functional Director and management teams on key decisions;
 Improving financial performance by leading the full planning and control cycle, including reporting, budgeting, and forecasting;
 Supporting and leading business development through business cases, investment plans, and acquisition activities;
 Working with the CFO and Finance Management Team as a member of the Global Business Control Lead Team;
 Strengthening collaboration and financial expertise among regional and local Business Controllers and Finance Managers.
 What you bring as our future colleague 
You have strong analytical and strategic skills and can turn financial insights into clear business choices. You build relationships easily and constructively challenge and influence senior stakeholders. You enjoy working in an international environment and take responsibility for shared results. In addition, you have:
 A relevant master’s degree in Finance, Business Economics, or a comparable field;
 Around 10 years of relevant experience in controlling and finance business partnering, preferably in a commercial environment;
 Experience working in an international and multicultural environment;
 Proven experience in stakeholder management and advising senior management;
 A strong understanding of financial and commercial processes on a global scale;
 Excellent command of English.
 Enza Zaden as your employer 
Enza Zaden is an international family-owned company that has been developing innovative vegetable varieties since 1938. Together with more than 3,300 colleagues worldwide, we work on vegetable seeds with better flavor, higher yields and strong resistances. We do this from our mission: “Breeding to feed the world.” Every day, more than 480 million people eat vegetables grown from our seeds, and that is something we are very proud of.
 We are passionate about our work and care about one another. Good ideas are given room to grow and together we keep moving forward. This is how we continue to grow and innovate, both as a company and as colleagues.
 What you can expect from us 
We believe it is important that you can grow in your work and feel good about what you do. That is why we invest in your development, well-being, and job satisfaction. Through our Great to Grow development program, our focus on vitality, and activities that bring colleagues together, we create a work environment where you can keep learning and contribute with energy and enjoyment. You can also count on:
 A position for 32-38 hours per week;
 A gross monthly salary between €6,943 and €9,919, based on a full-time workweek of 38 hours and aligned with your knowledge and experience;
 8.33% vacation allowance and an attractive annual bonus program of 15% of your annual salary, depending on your job level and company performance;
 25 vacation days, the option to purchase additional vacation days, and one paid vitality day per year, with extra vacation days granted as you get older;
 A laptop and mobile phone provided by Enza Zaden;
 A contribution toward overnight accommodation costs if you live farther away from Enza Zaden. This program applies to employees working for Enza Zaden in the Netherlands whose one-way commute exceeds 100 kilometers and 75 minutes;
 An attractive retirement plan, commuting reimbursement if you live more than 10 kilometers from your workplace and a remote work allowance when working partly from home in consultation with your manager;
 Opportunities for personal and professional growth through our Great to Grow development program, training courses, workshops, and e-learning platform;
 Plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues outside of your daily work through social events organized by the Staff Association, as well as Young Enza networking events, inspiration sessions, and social gatherings. We also host an annual summer barbecue, Christmas market and New Year’s reception;
 A strong focus on your health and well-being, including free fresh fruit, healthy lunch options at the office, a bike-to-work program, sports activities through enzActive, and mental well-being support through OpenUp.
 Let’s connect 
Looking for a career that grows with you? Apply using the application button. You will receive an automatic confirmation within a few minutes. We will let you know the next step within 10 business days.
 An assessment is possible part of the application process. This role cannot be filled on an interim basis.
 Do you have questions about the role or the application process? Please feel free to contact Sijmen Jansen, Corporate Recruiter, at si.jansen@enzazaden.nl.
 Enza Zaden is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate based on background, identity, or personal characteristics.
 Want to learn more about Enza Zaden? Visit our website .

industry:enza:JR105774.description:
Een gastvrije en goed georganiseerde lunchvoorziening maakt het verschil voor collega’s en bezoekers. Als Cateringmedewerker bij Enza Zaden zorg jij ervoor dat alles achter de schermen én aan de counters soepel verloopt. Van verse maaltijdsalades tot een goed gevulde broodjesbar: dankzij jouw inzet kunnen collega’s elke dag rekenen op een verzorgde en smakelijke lunch in een prettige werkomgeving.
 Maak het verschil als Cateringmedewerker
 Als Cateringmedewerker ben je samen met je collega’s verantwoordelijk voor de dagelijkse cateringvoorziening op onze locatie in Enkhuizen. Je werkt in een team van acht collega’s en zorgt ervoor dat de verschillende foodstations aantrekkelijk, goed gevuld en hygiënisch verzorgd zijn. Geen dag is hetzelfde: de ene keer bereid je verse gerechten voor, de andere keer ondersteun je bij een evenement of bijeenkomst. Met jouw inzet draag je bij aan een gastvrije omgeving waar collega’s en bezoekers zich welkom voelen.
 In deze functie houd je je bezig met:
 Het voorbereiden en bereiden van lunchgerechten, soepen, salades en broodjes;
 Het verzorgen van verschillende foodstations, zoals de fruit- en yoghurtbar, saladebar en warme gerechten;
 Het aanvullen, presenteren en uitserveren van producten;
 Het ondersteunen bij evenementen, borrels en buffetmomenten;
 Het uitvoeren van afwas- en schoonmaakwerkzaamheden volgens de geldende hygiënerichtlijnen;
 Het samenwerken met collega’s om een efficiënte en gastvrije cateringservice te bieden.
 Wat jij meebrengt als toekomstige collega  
Als Cateringmedewerker ben je praktisch ingesteld en houd je het hoofd koel tijdens drukke momenten. Je werkt graag samen, communiceert direct en duidelijk en weet prioriteiten te stellen wanneer het druk is. Daarnaast ben je flexibel, steek je graag de handen uit de mouwen en voel je je thuis in een dynamische werkomgeving waar teamwork centraal staat.
 Daarnaast heb je:
 Bij voorkeur ervaring in de catering, horeca of een vergelijkbare servicegerichte omgeving;
 Affiniteit met het bereiden en presenteren van verse voedingsmiddelen;
 Kennis van of oog voor hygiëne- en voedselveiligheidsrichtlijnen;
 Een stressbestendige en proactieve werkhouding;
 Een directe communicatiestijl en het vermogen om zelfstandig verantwoordelijkheid te nemen;
 Beschikbaarheid voor vijf werkdagen per week van 08:30 tot 14:30 uur en de flexibiliteit om incidenteel langer te werken tijdens evenementen, borrels of buffetten.
 Enza Zaden als jouw werkgever  
Enza Zaden is een internationaal familiebedrijf dat sinds 1938 innovatieve groenterassen ontwikkelt. Met meer dan 3.300 collega’s wereldwijd werken we aan groentezaden met een betere smaak, hogere opbrengsten en sterke resistenties. Dat doen we vanuit onze missie: ‘Breeding to feed the world’. Dagelijks eten ruim 480 miljoen mensen groenten die zijn geteeld uit onze zaden, iets waar we enorm trots op zijn.
 We hebben passie voor ons vak en oog voor elkaar. Goede ideeën krijgen bij ons de ruimte en samen zetten we stappen vooruit. Zo blijven we groeien en vernieuwen, als bedrijf én als collega’s. 
 Wat je van ons kunt verwachten   
We vinden het belangrijk dat je kunt groeien in je werk én je goed voelt in wat je doet. Daarom investeren we in jouw ontwikkeling, welzijn en werkplezier. Met ons Great to Grow ontwikkelprogramma, aandacht voor vitaliteit en activiteiten die collega’s samenbrengen, zorgen we voor een werkomgeving waarin je kunt blijven leren en met plezier kunt bijdragen. 
 Daarnaast kun je onder andere rekenen op: 
 Een functie voor 27,5 uur per week;  
 Een bruto maandsalaris tussen €2,652,- en €3,162,- (Schaal 2, CAO Tuinzaadbedrijven) bij een fulltime dienstverband van 38 uur, afgestemd op jouw kennis en ervaring;  
 8,33% vakantiegeld en een aantrekkelijke bonusregeling van 7,5% van je jaarsalaris, afhankelijk van je functieniveau en bedrijfsresultaat; 
 25 vakantiedagen, de mogelijkheid om extra vakantiedagen bij te kopen en één betaalde vitaliteitsdag per jaar, met extra dagen naarmate je ouder wordt;  
 Een aantrekkelijke pensioenregeling, reiskostenvergoeding als je verder dan 10 kilometer vanaf je werkplek woont en een thuiswerkvergoeding wanneer je in overleg met je manager deels thuis kunt werken; 
 Ruimte om jezelf te ontwikkelen via ons Great to Grow ontwikkelprogramma, opleidingen, cursussen en het e-learningplatform;  
 Volop mogelijkheden om collega’s te ontmoeten buiten je dagelijkse werk, bijvoorbeeld via uitjes en evenementen van de Personeelsvereniging en inspiratiesessies en borrels van Young Enza. Ook organiseren we jaarlijks onder andere een zomerbarbecue, kerstmarkt en nieuwjaarsborrel; 
 Aandacht voor jouw vitaliteit en welzijn met gratis vers fruit, de mogelijkheid om gezond te lunchen op kantoor, het fietsplan, sportactiviteiten via enzActive en mentale ondersteuning via OpenUp. 
 Laten we in contact komen  
 Zoek je een carrière die met je meegroeit? Solliciteer dan via de sollicitatieknop. Je ontvangt binnen enkele minuten een automatische bevestiging. Binnen 10 werkdagen laten we je weten wat de volgende stap is.
 Heb je vragen over de functie of het sollicitatieproces? Neem dan gerust contact op met Tamara Woudstra, Recruiter, via t.woudstra@enzazaden.nl 
 Enza Zaden is een werkgever die gelijke kansen biedt en discrimineert niet op basis van achtergrond, identiteit of persoonlijke kenmerken.
 Wil je meer weten over Enza Zaden? Neem dan een kijkje op onze website .

industry:enza:JR105780.description:
As Interim Global Manager Supply Planning, you will lead the global end-to-endsupply planning, shape and realize our business strategy, build strong capabilities and processes and lead a high-performing team. In doing so, you strengthen our global supply chain and support our purpose: Breeding to feed the world —delivering over 1,200 vegetable varieties worldwide within a collaborative, entrepreneurial family culture.
 Make a difference as Interim Global Manager Supply Planning 
As Interim Global Manager Supply Planning you will represent the Supply Chain within the cross functional Open Field Business Dynamic team. You are responsible for the end-to-end supply planning for the Open Field Business Dynamic. This means ensuring a strategic supply plan, including translation to and execution of a tactical and operational plan for all the crops and underlying crop segments to realize the Business Dynamics goals and objectives. You will lead the S&OP process in close alignment with Marketing and Sales, Demand Planning, Portfolio Management, R&D and Production. In this role, your work will include:
 A high degree of cross functional leadership;
 Foster a culture of growth for both crops and employees;
 Lead, motivate, coach, and develop the team to achieve optimal performance and goal alignment;
 Play a key role in building and expanding end-to-end planning capabilities;
 Set up and continuously improve planning processes and workflows;
 Drive the implementation of advanced planning systems, including long-term planning, inventory management, product quality management and order flow management.
 You will be reporting to the VP Supply Chain and actively contribute within the Business Dynamic team.
 What you bring as Interim Professional 
 As Interim Global Manager Supply Planning you bring excellent leadership skills and know how to effectively lead, motivate and coach a team. Your analytical mindset enables you to interpret and work with large data sets, helping you to anticipate challenges and solve complex problems. You combine strategic thinking with a hands-on approach, ensuring efficient planning processes and continuous improvement across the supply chain. In addition, you have:
 University degree in Supply chain management, Business Administration or Engineering
 12 or more years of experience in a similar role;
 Hands on experience in working with cross functional teams and leading your own team;
 Experience with complex stakeholder management;
 Excellent communication skills, proficient in English and Dutch.
 Enza Zaden as a company 
Enza Zaden is an international family-owned company that has been developing innovative vegetable varieties since 1938. Together with more than 3,300 colleagues worldwide, we work on vegetable seeds with better flavor, higher yield and strong resistances. We do this from our mission: “Breeding to feed the world.” Every day, more than 480 million people eat vegetables grown from our seeds, and that is something we are very proud of.
 We’re passionate about our work and care about one another. Good ideas are given room to grow and together we keep moving forward. This is how we continue to grow and innovate, both as a company and as colleagues.
 What you can expect from us 
We believe it is important that people can grow in their work and feel good about what they do. That is why we invest in development, well-being, and job satisfaction. Through our Great to Grow development program, our focus on vitality, and activities that bring colleagues together, we create a work environment where they can keep learning and contribute with energy and enjoyment. You can also count on:
 A six-month assignment for 38 hours per week, with the possibility of an extension;
 A gross monthly salary between € €7,774.05 and €11,105.78, based on a full-time workweek of 38 hours and aligned with your knowledge and experience;
 8.33% vacation allowance and an attractive annual bonus program of 15% of your annual salary, depending on your job level and company performance;
 25 vacation days, the option to purchase additional vacation days, and one paid vitality day per year, with extra vacation days granted as you get older;
 A laptop and mobile phone provided by Enza Zaden;
 A contribution toward overnight accommodation costs if you live farther away from Enza Zaden. This program applies to employees working for Enza Zaden in the Netherlands whose one-way commute exceeds 100 kilometers and 75 minutes;
 An attractive retirement plan, commuting reimbursement if you live more than 10 kilometers from your workplace and a remote work allowance when working partly from home in consultation with your manager;
 Opportunities for personal and professional growth through our Great to Grow development program, training courses, workshops, and e-learning platform;
 Plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues outside of your daily work through social events organized by the Staff Association, as well as Young Enza networking events, inspiration sessions, and social gatherings. We also host an annual summer barbecue, Christmas market and New Year’s reception;
 A strong focus on your health and well-being, including free fresh fruit, healthy lunch options at the office, a bike-to-work program, sports activities through enzActive, and mental well-being support through OpenUp.
 Let’s connect 
Are you an interim professional with extensive experience in Supply Planning? Share your cv using the application button . You will receive an automatic confirmation within a few minutes. We will let you know the next step within 10 business days.
Do you have questions about the role or the selection process? Please feel free to contact Esther Scharloo, Senior Recruiter at e.scharloo@enzazaden.nl .
