 You're at ease in collaborative, interdisciplinary settings, and you communicate and facilitate confidently with diverse groups;
 You take ownership and initiative, and are ready to lead when a project needs it;
 You're comfortable enough with coding, digital tools and AI applications to experiment with them and talk shop with technical collaborators;
 You're genuinely interested in the societal and political implications of data, AI, and data infrastructure;
 You can communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing;
 Experience with EU-funded or other large collaborative research projects is a strong plus, and some Dutch is an asset but not essential.
