 The DATAGOV Living Lab is part of a larger research programme investigating how data infrastructures are reshaping democratic governance, public institutions and citizen participation. Rather than a conventional laboratory, it is a space where researchers, practitioners, public institutions, civil society organisations, artists and citizens explore these transformations together, experimenting with alternative ways of researching and governing data and AI. You will join an interdisciplinary, international team that does not expect you to fit a single professional profile: you might come from an arts or cultural organisation, a civic technology initiative, or a design or innovation lab. What matters is your ability to move comfortably between the practical coordination of the Lab and active participation in designing, facilitating and developing its experimental programme, with considerable scope to bring your own ideas to its growth.
 The DATAGOV project at the University of Amsterdam is looking for a Lab Manager to coordinate and help develop the DATAGOV Living Lab, an experimental research environment focused on the relationship between data and AI infrastructures, governance and democracy.
 Shape a living lab for data, AI and democracy
