Join us!
 We are looking for temporary thesis supervisors with an affinity for both geography/urban geography and strong methodological skills. Specifically, candidates should be able to supervise an academic thesis, at both the bachelor and master level. Thesis supervision means having a group of 5-6 students at a time, meeting regularly with them, taking an interest in their own ideas through open discussion, and helping them to turn these interests into feasible research topics and a final thesis.
 What are you going to do
 Thesis supervision at the Master and Bachelor levels and in consultation small additional teaching tasks depending on availability and expertise.
 What do you have to offer
 A PhD in a field related to Human Geography, Planning or International Development Studies;
 Experience in Bachelor or Master level thesis supervision;
 Fluency in English and/or Dutch.
 Enthusiasm for working closely with students and helping them develop their ideas;
 Expertise in one or more the fields of spatial analysis, political geography, urban studies, climate change, migration, gender, urban planning and urban transformations or other related fields;
 Academic or professional expertise in the themes listed above as well as a professional or academic network which can be shared with students;
 Is willing to be flexible and adjust to new supervision styles in a short amount of time;
