 As Programme Manager Extracurricular Development, you lead the teams that shape these initiatives. You develop an integrated vision for extracurricular development within WUR. This role has a strong focus on professional leadership, strategic development and collaboration. You create an inspiring working environment for staff and ensure a strong, recognisable offering for students. You also strengthen ties with societal partners and contribute to positioning WUR as a university that prepares students for complex societal challenges. 
 You lead a team of approximately 9 FTE within Studium Generale and Student Challenges. From 2028, the Honours Programme will also join, growing the team to approximately 11 FTE. You create space for professionals to keep developing, encourage collaboration, and ensure the programmes continue to meet the needs of students and society. Together with education teams, colleagues within Student Life, Wellbeing & Inclusion, academic advisory boards and external partners, you develop new opportunities. You connect people, ideas and societal issues, and give the programmes a clear place within and beyond WUR. You report to the Dean of Education. 
