 working hours that can be arranged in consultation, allowing for an optimal work-life balance;
 sabbatical leave, study leave, and partially paid parental leave;
 a strong focus on vitality and well-being, with access to on-campus sports facilities at an attractive rate;
 a structural year-end bonus of 8.3%;
 an excellent pension scheme through ABP.
 Naturally, these excellent secondary employment benefits are accompanied by an appropriate salary. Depending on your experience, we offer a market-based salary ranging from a minimum of € 3,640, - to a maximum of € 5,132, - gross per month based on a full-time working week of 36 hours, in accordance with the Wageningen Research Collective Labour Agreement (Scale 9). Regarding the contract, we initially offer a one-year appointment with the intention of converting it into a permanent contract. Naturally, we are happy to discuss this with you should you have any questions.
