Project Controller
Your job
 Are you looking for a challenging position where you can grow? Would you like to develop your expertise in grant schemes and everything that comes with them? Wageningen University & Research (WUR) is looking for a Project Controller for 36 hours per week. Will you become our new colleague? 
 What are you going to do?
 As a Project Controller, you are responsible for the administration and financial management of research projects, including grant-funded projects. From budgeting through to final settlement, you translate between finance and research.
 Together with the Business Controller and project leaders, you ensure effective financial control and risk management of projects within several departments of the Agrotechnology & Food Sciences Group (AFSG). You have a comprehensive overview of the financial aspects of these projects. You identify potential risks at an early stage and take action where necessary. You also contribute to the implementation of internal control measures and provide critical input when assessing procedures.
 You coordinate and support (grant-funded) projects and manage their financial administration;
